#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133552 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133742 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0341b26-9c91-5b8a-a917-20129155e336" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Row Operation Equivalent To Left Multiplication by an Elementary Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "126c85b8-d721-5e7d-a3dc-df997bc0b9ce" :question/math-academy-id "e-4732" :question/problem "Consider ![](images/46/4632b2999b4578282c7f0d71fdf36004123551187fa9a6980051d7ff89f48296.svg) and a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$\nFind the row operation that, when applied to $A,$ is equivalent to multiplying $A$ by the given elementary matrix $E$ from the left." :question/worked-solution "The given matrix $E$ is obtained by taking the second row of $I$ and adding $7$ times the third row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+7{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary \nrow operation $R_2 :=R_2+7R_3$ to $A.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133553 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133743 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "09d8ec89-4d75-51ac-a870-1d2f8a1800ba" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix Left Multiplication Equivalent To a Given Row Operation"}] :question/id #uuid "f8eb89c4-1cca-5f8c-909c-31e9e0fc8412" :question/math-academy-id "e-4733" :question/problem "Suppose we are applying the elementary row operation $R_2:=R_2-2R_1$ to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$ What is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" :question/worked-solution "We need to find a matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation $R_2 := R_2-2R_1$ to $A.$\n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](images/a2/a23e35f367c6d8ca4bdbee47bacf9afca23dea031b0a647dda5067746bf45e46.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133554 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133744 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "00b69189-1ae1-5625-adfb-e5460845c776" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix Left Multiplication Equivalent To a Sequence of Row Operations"}] :question/id #uuid "6e47a532-ba7a-5692-961b-eabc743d74e6" :question/math-academy-id "e-4734" :question/problem "Suppose we are applying these two elementary row operations, in the given order, to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\nR_2\\leftrightarrow R_3, \\qquad\n\tR_1:=6R_1\n$$\n\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the two given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first operation is $R_2\\leftrightarrow R_3.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second operation is $R_1:=6R_1.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=6{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by $E_1$ on the left and get $E_1 A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](images/d2/d2425878812bb00748c5250dd877655a7d01faab33e148593be2a6c2de98ac4e.svg)\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to $E_1 A,$ we multiply by $E_2$ on the left and get $E_2 E_1 A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](images/c7/c741f5faf39a8bc1606d64e906162bbd5b67b3dfd88af2372f43e96736de6bb5.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555762 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133742 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0341b26-9c91-5b8a-a917-20129155e336" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Row Operation Equivalent To Left Multiplication by an Elementary Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2529a149-fb30-55fe-bdf8-5d56196dafd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555074} {:answer/id #uuid "5b667e85-23d7-57a6-b6f9-faa8ef1bf4ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555202} {:answer/id #uuid "95255e74-49c2-5fc5-9b5f-382b8d6441d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555354} {:answer/id #uuid "9d8106d0-0df0-5fa4-b131-de449ea45e78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-3{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555377} {:answer/id #uuid "c252ed9f-342e-57d8-9f1c-24b289a4beb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555469}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2529a149-fb30-55fe-bdf8-5d56196dafd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555074} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d8fe497-6500-5a3d-bec7-a1a5ff5c4b03" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555660}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0dc73948-1028-504a-8a43-9f0c9272154c" :question/math-academy-id "q-110462" :question/problem "Consider $E=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ and a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$ Find the row operation that, when applied to $A,$ is equivalent to multiplying $A$ by the given elementary matrix $E$ from the left." :question/worked-solution "The given matrix $E$ is obtained by multiplying the second row of ${I}_{3}$ by $-\\frac{1}{3}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary \nrow operation ${R}_{2}:=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2}$ to $A.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555791 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133742 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0341b26-9c91-5b8a-a917-20129155e336" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Row Operation Equivalent To Left Multiplication by an Elementary Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d56313c-529d-5eca-ad82-a0508fc3fb86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:=7{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555051} {:answer/id #uuid "6b2ad059-1df4-54c9-bd82-322256b36f80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+7{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555244} {:answer/id #uuid "c347b5a9-9ae2-58bb-84c8-a9d578f6c1af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{7}{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555472} {:answer/id #uuid "d2c4f9e3-00fb-5fad-b454-4772f485d6df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+7{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555499} {:answer/id #uuid "ed1261c8-d574-56d6-a7fa-90c22ec256e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-7{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555583}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2c4f9e3-00fb-5fad-b454-4772f485d6df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+7{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555499} :answer-field/id #uuid "dde3abf0-6177-5679-8941-b43d0716b340" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555747}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3a8b7714-d243-5a18-865d-0e2cf918670b" :question/math-academy-id "q-110463" :question/problem "Consider $E=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ and a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$ Find the row operation that, when applied to $A,$ is equivalent to multiplying $A$ by the given elementary matrix $E$ from the left." :question/worked-solution "The given matrix $E$ is obtained by taking the third row of ${I}_{3}$ and adding $7$ times the first row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+7{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+7{R}_{1}$ to $A.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555812 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133743 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "09d8ec89-4d75-51ac-a870-1d2f8a1800ba" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix Left Multiplication Equivalent To a Given Row Operation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43dc20c6-76f4-5f40-a083-a68fff62c7a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555144} {:answer/id #uuid "89b8174c-7ba1-5290-9544-eefeb40cdcfb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555320} {:answer/id #uuid "9114918e-0981-5c69-81c4-192ab15eea5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555341} {:answer/id #uuid "e4c1d932-65e6-50ad-8efd-0e962ff77a32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555561} {:answer/id #uuid "e700ce2b-8be4-5604-877b-03482d66f546" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555567}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e700ce2b-8be4-5604-877b-03482d66f546" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555567} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ccaad93-79fb-5e66-a9e7-978681d178cb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555691}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5e29c468-7ba6-5997-83d8-49458f8bde8e" :question/math-academy-id "q-110470" :question/problem "Suppose that the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{3}$ is applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$ What is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" :question/worked-solution "We need to find a matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{3}$ to $A.$\n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+2{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247126 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133743 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "09d8ec89-4d75-51ac-a870-1d2f8a1800ba" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix Left Multiplication Equivalent To a Given Row Operation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e7315f0-8f33-584d-a228-448a96c382a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244443} {:answer/id #uuid "5170a4b6-2e55-540e-a9fb-a40ab98bfacd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245037} {:answer/id #uuid "63386325-897f-52d1-8442-84f7f16497fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 &